description.narrative:
25 Bolivian PhD students in the sandwich PhD program with Swedish universities are progressing in their research within the research areas:
1. Agriculture and food;
2. Technological and productive development;
3.  Water and soil;
4.  Energy, renewable raw materials and mining;
5.  Health, and;
6.  Socioeconomics, education and culture.

In 2023, the program resulted in 23 scientific publications with potential to have an effect on development and poverty reduction in Bolivia.

The final research results of the research supported by Sida in the present phase will be published in articles and monographs when the PhD students defend their dissertations.
